<%- include('header') %><main class="reading"><div class="eyebrow">CONNECTION GUIDE</div><h1>Pick up your<br>next conversation.</h1><p class="lede">Save useful context in one Sesame call or chat, then retrieve it in the next. The same voice and connection are enough.</p><section><h2>Connect from Sesame</h2><ol class="steps"><li><span>01</span><div><h3>Open Apps</h3><p>In the Sesame app, go to <strong>Agent Hub → Apps</strong> and add an external MCP.</p></div></li><li><span>02</span><div><h3>Paste the address</h3><div class="copy-row"><code><%= config.resource %></code><button type="button" class="copy-button" data-copy="<%= config.resource %>">Copy ↗</button></div></div></li><li><span>03</span><div><h3>Sign in and label the connection</h3><p>Create a Brain account or sign in. Choose a label for the connection, approve access, then return to Sesame. The label attributes saved records; it does not require a separate assistant or brain.</p></div></li><li><span>04</span><div><h3>Save now. Resume next time.</h3><p>Ask Sesame to save a useful detail in Brain. In a new call or chat, use the same connection and ask: “Resume from Brain. Where did we leave off?”</p></div></li></ol><p class="callout">Brain only knows what is sent through its tools. It does not import your existing Sesame history or capture every spoken word. Ask it to save the useful details and resume from Brain next time.</p></section><section><h2>Try saying</h2><div class="examples"><blockquote>“Save in Brain that I take the 7:40 train.”</blockquote><blockquote>“Before we finish, save the key decisions and open questions in Brain.”</blockquote><blockquote>“Resume from Brain. Where did we leave off?”</blockquote><blockquote>“Open my weekend project in Brain. What changed since last time?”</blockquote></div></section><section><h2>A dashboard for your saved context</h2><p>Sign in to <a href="/dashboard">your dashboard</a> to explore saved memories, add a note or fact, ask Brain a question, start background work, read overnight updates, and download saved files. Your default brain is enough to start. If you use additional workspaces, the selector keeps their records separate.</p></section><section><h2>Keep a living project between conversations</h2><p>Start a <a href="/dashboard/projects">living project</a> with a name and a goal. Keep its constraints, decisions, questions, milestones, tasks, and artifacts together. In your next call or chat, ask the same voice to open that project in Brain and check what changed.</p><p>Every saved change has a version and an actor. Source references show where a detail came from. If an assistant proposes a correction to information you confirmed, your current version stays in place until you approve or reject the proposal.</p><p>Changing a constraint or decision flags dependent items for review. It does not automatically approve those items or publish anything. A retrieval receipt means an assistant fetched that version from Brain; it does not verify a native call boundary or mean Sesame’s internal memory was rewritten.</p></section><section><h2>Think now. Keep going later.</h2><p>Ask your assistant to <strong>think</strong> when a question needs reasoning or a wider memory. Ask it to <strong>do</strong> something when the work needs more time. Background results are saved in your brain and can be retrieved in your next conversation; you can also read them in the dashboard.</p><p>Ask for <strong>resume</strong> at the start of a call or chat to retrieve current saved context, even when you return a few minutes later. An initial Brain request can also return this context automatically. When a conversation goes quiet or ends, Brain can save an automatic snapshot. After an active day, overnight reflections revisit the record, check interpretations, and describe what changed.</p><p>These features use connected reasoning providers and a daily thinking allowance. <a href="/privacy">Read how your context is used.</a></p></section><section><h2>What your assistants can do</h2><dl class="tool-list"><div><dt>Resume a conversation</dt><dd><code>resume</code> retrieves saved context, the current project, open work and waiting results without needing a second connection or a long idle gap.</dd></div><div><dt>Think with context</dt><dd><code>think</code> returns a focused answer using the memory in this brain.</dd></div><div><dt>Work between conversations</dt><dd><code>do</code>, <code>job_status</code>, and <code>jobs_list</code> start and follow background work.</dd></div><div><dt>Close a conversation</dt><dd><code>end_session</code> closes the Brain check-in before goodbye. When authorized AI is available, it can also summarize the recorded activity.</dd></div><div><dt>Get oriented</dt><dd><code>whoami</code> shows their identity, connected assistants, and waiting items.</dd></div><div><dt>Exchange notes</dt><dd><code>leave_note</code>, <code>inbox</code>, <code>read_notes</code>, and <code>mark_notes_read</code> pass messages to one assistant or everyone.</dd></div><div><dt>Hand off work</dt><dd><code>handoff</code>, <code>accept_handoff</code>, and <code>complete_handoff</code> pass a task with context and a completion note.</dd></div><div><dt>Remember together</dt><dd><code>remember</code>, <code>recall</code>, and <code>forget</code> maintain shared facts about you.</dd></div><div><dt>Keep a backup</dt><dd><code>save_snapshot</code>, <code>list_snapshots</code>, and <code>get_snapshot</code> save and retrieve assistant-written memory exports.</dd></div><div><dt>See what changed</dt><dd><code>activity</code> shows recent actions across your connected assistants.</dd></div></dl></section><section><h2>Your account, under your control</h2><p>New accounts can use shared memory and projects immediately. Hosted thinking and background work need account approval. In <a href="/account/recovery">account settings</a>, generate recovery codes so you have a way to reset a forgotten password. Each code works once.</p></section><section class="faq"><h2>A few good questions</h2><details open><summary>Do I need more than one connection?</summary><p>No. One connection can save and retrieve context across conversations with the same voice. Additional clients or connections are optional. Their labels provide attribution and access controls; they do not define separate people or prove native call boundaries.</p></details><details><summary>Can Claude or ChatGPT connect too?</summary><p>Yes, if your client supports external OAuth MCP servers. Add the same MCP address, sign in with the same account, and choose Other with a name such as <code>claude</code> or <code>chatgpt</code>. Availability depends on your client and plan.</p></details><details><summary>How do I export or delete my data?</summary><p>Open <a href="/account">your account</a>. Export downloads one JSON file. Clear brain content resets the selected brain while preserving your account and connections. Delete account asks for confirmation and removes your live data and connections immediately. Saved workspace files can be downloaded separately from the dashboard. Recovery backups expire within 14 days.</p></details><details><summary>What if I picked the wrong assistant?</summary><p>Rename the connection in your account. Previously written notes retain their original author labels; the connection uses its new identity for future requests.</p></details><details><summary>Will assistants check automatically?</summary><p>Brain’s tools ask Sesame to resume saved context when a conversation starts. You can ask explicitly: “Resume from Brain.” Brain does not push notifications into Sesame or read a call that never uses its tools.</p></details><details><summary>What if Sesame cannot connect?</summary><p>Verify the address and that you are using the same Brain account. Client behavior may change. Include the approximate time and app version when <a href="https://github.com/Oscar-G13/sesame-brain/issues">reporting an issue</a>; never post passwords, tokens, or private memory.</p></details></section><p class="small muted">Requires an OAuth-capable MCP client. Brain is unofficial and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Sesame AI Inc.</p></main><%- include('footer') %>
